ight=1` (`num_y=1`): single block launched\n  - Allocates intermediate buffer based on `buffer_size` and `num_y` (line 175)\n\n**`LogupMleBatchBuilder` (lines 259-408):**\n- Filters traces with interactions (line 279)\n- Same block assignment logic\n- Builds `LogupCtx` per trace (lines 312-363)\n\n**For Height-1 Traces:**\n- `num_y = 1` → `threads_per_block = min(1, 128) = 1`\n- One block per trace\n- Minimal intermediate buffers\n- Very efficient kernel launch\n\n---\n\n### **7. Critical Line Numbers and File Paths**\n\n| Component | File | Lines |\n|-----------|------|-------|\n| Struct definition | `mod.rs` | 720-788 |\n| Initialization | `mod.rs` | 857-915 |\n| Ping-pong allocation | `mod.rs` | 626-647 |\n| `sumcheck_polys_batch_eval` start | `mod.rs` | 1576 |\n| Case A.1 (height-1 eval) | `mod.rs` | 1641-1677 |\n| Case B partition | `mod.rs` | 1639-1732 |\n| Interpolation kernel | `mod.rs` | 1766-1772 |\n| `fold_mle_evals` start | `mod.rs` | 2052 |\n| `fold_pingpong` function | `mod.rs` | 2058-2145 |\n| Partition point (height==1) | `mod.rs` | 2064 |\n| Non-foldable skip | `mod.rs` | 2142 |\n| `evaluate_zerocheck_batched` | `batch_mle.rs` | 414 |\n| `evaluate_logup_batched` | `batch_mle.rs` | 505 |\n| Monomial threshold partition | `batch_mle.rs` | 516-519 |\n| Height-1 eval special case | `batch_mle.rs` | 533-541 |\n| `ZerocheckMleBatchBuilder::new` | `batch_mle.rs` | 127 |\n| `LogupMleBatchBuilder::new` | `batch_mle.rs` | 273 |\n\n---\n\n### **Key Insights**\n\n1. **Height-1 traces are deeply optimized:**\n   - They skip the GPU fold kernel entirely via `partition_point()`\n   - Never copied between ping-pong buffers\n   - Evaluated directly at single points via monomial batches\n   - Results cached in `*_tilde_evals` for subsequent rounds\n\n2. **Two evaluation paths converge:**\n   - **Early (Case B):** Interpolation → batch MLE kernels\n   - **Late (Case A):** Direct monomial kernels\n   - Both handle `num_y=1` efficiently via threshold partitioning\n\n3. 