{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01L1YvxEx6aAYbKU2taGvE4M","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Dd3uQDjVwmdRT3AVW1Wjie","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-15-0100-batch-global-gkr-input-eval\n\nReplace per-AIR GLOBAL-mode GKR input evaluation kernel launches with a single batched descriptor-array kernel for small AIRs (height ≤ TASK_SIZE). Currently each of ~300 GLOBAL AIRs at APC 300 launches a 256-block kernel with TASK_SIZE=65536 threads regardless of actual height, wasting 90-99% of threads for small AIRs and serializing execution across 8 streams. A batched kernel with per-AIR descriptors processes all small GLOBAL AIRs in one launch with right-sized block counts, enabling GPU-native block scheduling instead of coarse-grained stream scheduling, and eliminating ~300 kernel launch overheads per segment.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":906,"cache_read_input_tokens":192404,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":906},"output_tokens":42,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c4196e5-21f2-4e88-ab6f-fb2d2870d4db","uuid":"6ea3887a-be41-4dd2-8b08-33856e03c9b0"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Dd3uQDjVwmdRT3AVW1Wjie","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c4196e5-21f2-4e88-ab6f-fb2d2870d4db","uuid":"1e337afe-5568-4db8-b67a-852a156ebe47","timestamp":"2026-04-14T23:00:14.912Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-15-0100-batch-global-gkr-input-eval\n\nReplace per-AIR GLOBAL-mode GKR input evaluation kernel launches with a single batched descriptor-array kernel for small AIRs (height ≤ TASK_SIZE). Currently each of ~300 GLOBAL AIRs at APC 300 launches a 256-block kernel with TASK_SIZE=65536 threads regardless of actual height, wasting 90-99% of threads for small AIRs and serializing execution across 8 streams. A batched kernel with per-AIR descriptors processes all small GLOBAL AIRs in one launch with right-sized block counts, enabling GPU-native block scheduling instead of coarse-grained stream scheduling, and eliminating ~300 kernel launch overheads per segment.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1,"newLines":3,"lines":["-# 2026-04-15-0030-drain-gpu-pipeline-before-stark","+# 2026-04-15-0100-batch-global-gkr-input-eval"," ","-The STARK excl trace timing span includes ~150-200ms of GPU pipeline stall at APC 300 caused by async trace generation kernels (especially `apc_apply_bus_kernel`, 609ms GPU time) that are still executing when the STARK prover begins. Per-segment analysis shows segment 0's Trace Commit is 164ms but actual commit work is only ~35ms — the remaining ~130ms is waiting for trace gen GPU kernels to drain. Adding a `current_stream_sync()` before the `stark_prove_excluding_trace` timing span ensures the metric accurately measures STARK work and eliminates GPU resource contention between trace gen and STARK kernels. This disproportionately helps APC 300 (where trace gen launches many more async GPU kernels) vs APC 0 (where trace gen is simpler), directly improving the APC 0/APC 300 scaling ratio.","+Replace per-AIR GLOBAL-mode GKR input evaluation kernel launches with a single batched descriptor-array kernel for small AIRs (height ≤ TASK_SIZE). Currently each of ~300 GLOBAL AIRs at APC 300 launches a 256-block kernel with TASK_SIZE=65536 threads regardless of actual height, wasting 90-99% of threads for small AIRs and serializing execution across 8 streams. A batched kernel with per-AIR descriptors processes all small GLOBAL AIRs in one launch with right-sized block counts, enabling GPU-native block scheduling instead of coarse-grained stream scheduling, and eliminating ~300 kernel launch overheads per segment."]}],"originalFile":"# 2026-04-15-0030-drain-gpu-pipeline-before-stark\n\nThe STARK excl trace timing span includes ~150-200ms of GPU pipeline stall at APC 300 caused by async trace generation kernels (especially `apc_apply_bus_kernel`, 609ms GPU time) that are still executing when the STARK prover begins. Per-segment analysis shows segment 0's Trace Commit is 164ms but actual commit work is only ~35ms — the remaining ~130ms is waiting for trace gen GPU kernels to drain. Adding a `current_stream_sync()` before the `stark_prove_excluding_trace` timing span ensures the metric accurately measures STARK work and eliminates GPU resource contention between trace gen and STARK kernels. This disproportionately helps APC 300 (where trace gen launches many more async GPU kernels) vs APC 0 (where trace gen is simpler), directly improving the APC 0/APC 300 scaling ratio.\n"}}
