{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EfgS9H9tUXE2Lr5QzVFroN","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-15-0100-batch-global-gkr-input-eval\n2\t\n3\tReplace per-AIR GLOBAL-mode GKR input evaluation kernel launches with a single batched descriptor-array kernel for small AIRs (height ≤ TASK_SIZE). Currently each of ~300 GLOBAL AIRs at APC 300 launches a 256-block kernel with TASK_SIZE=65536 threads regardless of actual height, wasting 90-99% of threads for small AIRs and serializing execution across 8 streams. A batched kernel with per-AIR descriptors processes all small GLOBAL AIRs in one launch with right-sized block counts, enabling GPU-native block scheduling instead of coarse-grained stream scheduling, and eliminating ~300 kernel launch overheads per segment.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01LAUawgWZuvpEDpDTF67JV1","session_id":"5c4196e5-21f2-4e88-ab6f-fb2d2870d4db","uuid":"51394cd5-f26f-47c6-bf97-e888abcf6ddb","timestamp":"2026-04-14T23:08:01.190Z"}
